  "corrections": [
    {"was": "the packet brief: route the script's bindings so the ships the script addresses receive real attackmove / moveto orders and the ship motion moves them",
     "is": "the bindings run and the orders are real MT_COMMAND messages with the right command object, ordinal, flags and descriptor, but they stop at 00816e30's own arm 00816f7c, which is projected nowhere. No scripted order reaches a weapon director slot and no ship moves under one.",
     "evidence": "src/cruise_command.cpp's command_takes_movement_fall_through selects cruise, stop and moveonpath only; docs/CRUISE_COMMAND.md reads 00816f7c..00817330 in pseudocode and projects none of it; milestone 2l follow-up 6 names the packet entity_command_arms."},
    {"was": "the packet brief: vehicle class preload 0095c640 has a reconstruction on main",
     "is": "it does not. python tools/bsp.py lookup 0095c640 answers FUN_0095c640 with no ledger name, and the address is leased to agent/cc2-scene-traffic-groups.",
     "evidence": "the ledger lookup and python tools/bsp.py lease list"},
    {"was": "milestone 2l: the mission's own order function addresses 21 of the 32 created instances through ten bindings that are all host records",
     "is": "six of the ten now run their reconstructed bodies (SetSkillLevel, SetRoleAvailable, JoinFormation, NavigatorMoveToRange, RepairEnable, NavigatorAttackMove). The other four rows of the mission's ten, NavigatorSetTorpedoEvasion, NavigatorSetAvoidLandCollision, SetInvincible and SetFireTarget, are other packets' and keep the record.",
     "evidence": "the run log's `binding <name> ... (reconstructed body)` lines and summary mission script bindings"},
    {"was": "docs/MISSION_LOAD_HOSTS.md's interface names reset_network_slots, reset_objective_list and rebuild_scripted_name_list",
     "is": "the executable's load walk accepts both those spellings and the corrected ones (erase_native_string_set, rebuild_avoid_zone_table, record_script_function_baseline), because the rename is landing on main at the same time.",
     "evidence": "docs/MISSION_LOAD_HOSTS.md headline table"},
    {"was": "the weather-descriptor pass would select a descriptor for the selected mission",
     "is": "this installation's scripts/datatables/weather.lua opens a --[[ block on line 2 and closes it on line 136, its last content line, so every authored entry is inside the comment and Weathers evaluates to {}. No mission on this installation selects a weather descriptor.",
     "evidence": "the shipped file, and the run's `weather pass: ... carries 0 entry(ies)` line"},
    {"was": "milestone 2l's --order takes throttle=<f>,rudder=<f> or a command name",
     "is": "it also takes speed=<m/s>, the store luaMW_SetShipSpeed 00890d30 makes on the controlled unit's navigator parameter block. It writes no throttle: docs/UNIT_COMMANDED_SPEED.md establishes that +28h is the mission clock and that 00836e59 is what turns an active pair into a cruise rather than a stop.",
     "evidence": "docs/UNIT_COMMANDED_SPEED.md sections 'The producers, read' and 'The command stages'"}
  ],

